473
00:22:07.955 --> 00:22:10.783
I didn't know
that Benny had dementia.

474
00:22:12.058 --> 00:22:13.885
It's kinda good that
he went the way he did.

475
00:22:13.886 --> 00:22:15.437
it was probably
a kindness of God.

476
00:22:15.438 --> 00:22:18.195
It-it would've killed us
to watch him go through that.

477
00:22:18.196 --> 00:22:20.541
Enough to take matters
into your own hands?

478
00:22:22.369 --> 00:22:23.954
The night Benny died.

479
00:22:23.955 --> 00:22:26.713
I was at
the Mount Dennis Legion.

480
00:22:26.714 --> 00:22:28.540
Charity poker game.

481
00:22:28.541 --> 00:22:29.851
You know what?

482
00:22:29.852 --> 00:22:31.161
Here.

483
00:22:31.162 --> 00:22:34.816
Enjoy 'em... on your way out.

484
00:22:34.817 --> 00:22:36.644
Well. his grief seemed real.

485
00:22:36.645 --> 00:22:38.575
but. uh. I once
knew a mob guy

486
00:22:38.576 --> 00:22:40.161
who swore he never
beat his wife.

487
00:22:40.162 --> 00:22:42.299
even when I found him
standing over her dead body.

488
00:22:42.300 --> 00:22:44.885
Yeah. well.
empty visitor's log

489
00:22:44.886 --> 00:22:47.575
has the mob written
all over it.

490
00:22:47.576 --> 00:22:49.540
Still begs the question. though.

491
00:22:49.541 --> 00:22:51.162
Who else was left off?

492
00:22:52.438 --> 00:22:54.609
So you're still
saying that Benny had

493
00:22:54.610 --> 00:22:56.437
no visitors
for an entire year?

494
00:22:56.438 --> 00:22:58.230
I showed you
the visitor's log.

495
00:22:58.231 --> 00:22:59.816
Okay. see.
that's the thing about being

496
00:22:59.817 --> 00:23:01.782
married to the mob. Charlotte.

497
00:23:01.783 --> 00:23:04.092
It makes telling the truth
a little harder. doesn't it?

498
00:23:04.093 --> 00:23:06.609
Mob boss shows up
with his best friend.

499
00:23:06.610 --> 00:23:08.644
tells you to look after him.

500
00:23:08.645 --> 00:23:11.058
Well. I bet you're
gonna do what he says.

501
00:23:11.886 --> 00:23:14.333
No. we get it.
These are scary people.

502
00:23:14.334 --> 00:23:16.057
But you...

503
00:23:16.058 --> 00:23:18.506
You run a tight ship. huh?

504
00:23:18.507 --> 00:23:20.472
Look at that. Jealous.

505
00:23:21.645 --> 00:23:24.126
So what are the names?
- To be clear.

506
00:23:24.127 --> 00:23:26.402
all I did was agree
to keep the log empty.

507
00:23:26.403 --> 00:23:29.230
Okay. so who
do we not know about?

508
00:23:29.231 --> 00:23:32.023
A few weeks ago. my assistant
didn't get the memo

509
00:23:32.024 --> 00:23:34.609
about not entering
Benny's visitors.

510
00:23:34.610 --> 00:23:38.402
She entered a name into the log.
I arrived and--

511
00:23:38.403 --> 00:23:39.541
Deleted it.

512
00:23:40.955 --> 00:23:42.540
What was the name?

513
00:23:42.541 --> 00:23:43.920
I don't remember
the last name.

514
00:23:43.921 --> 00:23:46.058
but the first name's Ethan.

515
00:23:46.955 --> 00:23:51.471
So. no Ethans associated
with mob hits in the 90s.

516
00:23:51.472 --> 00:23:55.230
And nothing in the aughts
or the teens.

517
00:23:55.231 --> 00:23:58.231
Nothing in Hamilton.
nothing in Montreal.

518
00:23:58.990 --> 00:24:01.471
What about civilian murders?

519
00:24:01.472 --> 00:24:04.057
Maybe this wasn't
connected to a mob hit.

520
00:24:06.852 --> 00:24:08.126
Okay.

521
00:24:09.886 --> 00:24:11.471
Whoa.

522
00:24:11.472 --> 00:24:15.471
Uh. not exactly a civilian.
but narcotics officer.

523
00:24:15.472 --> 00:24:19.161
Vincent O'Hagen.
was murdered on Lake Simcoe.

524
00:24:19.162 --> 00:24:22.299
Uh. case file says that Benny
was briefly a suspect

525
00:24:22.300 --> 00:24:24.195
due to the gun that was used.
but then it got

526
00:24:24.196 --> 00:24:26.920
attributed to a string
of B&Es. but...

527
00:24:26.921 --> 00:24:29.920
Survived by his wife.
Angela O'Hagen.

528
00:24:29.921 --> 00:24:31.852
and son. Ethan O'Hagen.

529
00:24:33.334 --> 00:24:37.023
Okay. Ethan O'Hagen works in
corrections as a social worker.

530
00:24:37.024 --> 00:24:41.437
So we got the son of a.
of a slain police officer.

531
00:24:41.438 --> 00:24:44.506
working with hardened criminals.
His father's death. unsolved.

532
00:24:44.507 --> 00:24:47.161
Maybe Ethan hoped to find out
who killed his father

533
00:24:47.162 --> 00:24:50.195
by working with the only people
in the world who would know.

534
00:24:51.748 --> 00:24:53.023
Other killers.

535
00:24:53.024 --> 00:24:55.264
Maybe he finally found
the right suspect.

536
00:25:04.162 --> 00:25:06.989
So. Ethan.
who told you that Benny Cohen

537
00:25:06.990 --> 00:25:09.230
killed your father?
- Benny who?

538
00:25:09.231 --> 00:25:11.816
Ah. "Benny who."
Your father was a cop

539
00:25:11.817 --> 00:25:15.575
and he was murdered at a fishing
cabin on Lake Simcoe.

540
00:25:15.576 --> 00:25:18.057
Wasn't even on the job.
just trying to relax.

541
00:25:18.058 --> 00:25:22.195
catch a few carp.
It was a senseless. awful murder

542
00:25:22.196 --> 00:25:24.816
and you wanted revenge.
- I said I don't know any Benny.

543
00:25:24.817 --> 00:25:26.713
Well. the staff
at Gracewood Manor

544
00:25:26.714 --> 00:25:30.575
said that you visited Benny
in his suite. three weeks ago.

545
00:25:30.576 --> 00:25:32.471
Do you wanna keep
playing this game?

546
00:25:36.576 --> 00:25:38.506
One thing I've learned
on the job.

547
00:25:38.507 --> 00:25:39.747
cellmates talk.

548
00:25:39.748 --> 00:25:41.265
One of them squawked. huh?

549
00:25:42.748 --> 00:25:44.471
You've been doing this job.
what. five years?

550
00:25:44.472 --> 00:25:46.885
That's a lot of dangerous
men you talk to.

551
00:25:46.886 --> 00:25:49.438
Did you ask them all?
Wouldn't you?

552
00:25:50.231 --> 00:25:52.126
If you thought you could find
out who killed your father?

553
00:25:52.127 --> 00:25:54.506
Sure. he was your hero.
It became an obsession.

554
00:25:54.507 --> 00:25:55.885
You wanted justice.

555
00:25:55.886 --> 00:25:57.126
Hero...

556
00:25:57.127 --> 00:25:58.023
Right.

557
00:25:58.024 --> 00:25:59.609
He was a decorated officer.

558
00:25:59.610 --> 00:26:01.057
He--
- Look.

559
00:26:01.058 --> 00:26:02.644
Everything
you're saying is true.

560
00:26:02.645 --> 00:26:05.402
Yes. I wanted to find
my father's killer

561
00:26:05.403 --> 00:26:08.300
and yes. I planned
to kill him when I did.

562
00:26:09.645 --> 00:26:11.713
So...

563
00:26:11.714 --> 00:26:13.506
Ethan.

564
00:26:13.507 --> 00:26:14.679
Did you?

565
00:26:15.955 --> 00:26:17.333
I couldn't.

566
00:26:17.334 --> 00:26:18.989
I went to see Benny
at the home.

567
00:26:18.990 --> 00:26:20.990
I confronted him
about everything.

568
00:26:22.369 --> 00:26:23.678
It was so weird.

569
00:26:23.679 --> 00:26:25.299
Benny didn't duck from it.

570
00:26:25.300 --> 00:26:27.782
He admitted to killing
my father.

571
00:26:27.783 --> 00:26:29.369
He was regretful.

572
00:26:30.334 --> 00:26:31.782
Atoning. even.

573
00:26:31.783 --> 00:26:33.782
He told me things about
my father I never knew.

574
00:26:33.783 --> 00:26:35.333
Like what?

575
00:26:35.334 --> 00:26:37.609
Like the fact that my dad
was on the mafia payroll.

576
00:26:37.610 --> 00:26:39.162
Excuse me?

577
00:26:40.334 --> 00:26:42.885
Yeah. I. uh...

578
00:26:42.886 --> 00:26:44.851
I threw up after
Benny told me that one.

579
00:26:46.334 --> 00:26:48.333
But after I thought about it.
it all made sense.

580
00:26:48.334 --> 00:26:50.954
My dad had been taking money
from the Galatti family

581
00:26:50.955 --> 00:26:53.471
since he graduated
from police college.

582
00:26:53.472 --> 00:26:57.265
Ethan. did Benny tell you why
the mob wanted your father dead?

583
00:26:58.438 --> 00:27:01.437
Yeah. I hear some stash house
that got held up back in 2010.

584
00:27:01.438 --> 00:27:03.402
Yeah. James Town towers.

585
00:27:03.403 --> 00:27:04.954
The masked assailant. uh.

586
00:27:04.955 --> 00:27:06.885
took down three
Calabrian soldiers

587
00:27:06.886 --> 00:27:08.299
and two innocent bystanders.

588
00:27:08.300 --> 00:27:10.678
One of them. a six-year-old kid.

589
00:27:10.679 --> 00:27:12.678
It was my father.

590
00:27:17.369 --> 00:27:20.299
Apparently.
Dad felt he wasn't being

591
00:27:20.300 --> 00:27:24.161
paid enough. so. uh...

592
00:27:24.162 --> 00:27:26.506
He decided to get himself
a little cash bonus

593
00:27:26.507 --> 00:27:27.541
before Christmas.

594
00:27:29.886 --> 00:27:31.230
I spent my whole life.

595
00:27:31.231 --> 00:27:34.369
trying to get justice
for a good man that. um...

596
00:27:35.886 --> 00:27:37.610
Well. he never existed.

597
00:27:39.714 --> 00:27:42.507
Who was Vincent O'Hagen's
partner who was killed?

598
00:27:43.817 --> 00:27:45.402
Ethan knew we were coming.

599
00:27:45.403 --> 00:27:47.610
Maybe he still
has a partner in the force.

600
00:27:49.369 --> 00:27:50.817
Jesus.

601
00:27:55.576 --> 00:27:57.024
Okay.

602
00:27:57.817 --> 00:28:00.679
God gave him one face.
he gave himself another.

603
00:28:08.817 --> 00:28:10.989
What can I get you.
Detective Novak?

604
00:28:10.990 --> 00:28:12.678
Uh. is your.
is your husband here?

605
00:28:12.679 --> 00:28:14.126
- No.
- Oh.

606
00:28:14.127 --> 00:28:15.678
Can I give him a message?

607
00:28:15.679 --> 00:28:17.333
Yeah. sure.
I just wanted to say

608
00:28:17.334 --> 00:28:19.816
how sorry I was to hear
about Benny Cohen. Really.

609
00:28:19.817 --> 00:28:22.851
Benny was a good man.
Knew how to keep his mouth shut.

610
00:28:22.852 --> 00:28:24.920
At least until recently.
I heard he was getting

611
00:28:24.921 --> 00:28:27.575
a little sloppy?
- You want to get to the point?

612
00:28:27.576 --> 00:28:29.471
Sure. If Benny
happened to mention anything

613
00:28:29.472 --> 00:28:31.264
to you or your husband
about me.

614
00:28:31.265 --> 00:28:32.747
I suggest you just forget it.

615
00:28:32.748 --> 00:28:34.990
Or at least
keep it to yourselves.

616
00:28:36.921 --> 00:28:39.783
There are plenty more photos
where that came from.

617
00:28:53.748 --> 00:28:55.540
Walsh. come on. you gotta pass
the ball sometime!

618
00:28:55.541 --> 00:28:56.885
I'm open!

619
00:28:56.886 --> 00:29:00.092
- Put it up. put it up!
- Hopkins. it's all you.

620
00:29:00.093 --> 00:29:01.783
Don't let me down.

621
00:29:04.058 --> 00:29:06.437
Detectives.
any news on Benny Cohen?

622
00:29:06.438 --> 00:29:09.989
Uh. Ethan O'Hagen.
uh. your former partner.

623
00:29:09.990 --> 00:29:11.541
Vincent. um...

624
00:29:12.507 --> 00:29:14.575
Benny killed Vincent.

625
00:29:14.576 --> 00:29:18.195
Ethan found out
and wanted revenge.

626
00:29:18.196 --> 00:29:21.678
Ethan? Guys.
There is no way.

627
00:29:21.679 --> 00:29:24.437
You and Vincent were partners
for what. eight years?

628
00:29:24.438 --> 00:29:27.057
Were you close?
- Come on. guys.

629
00:29:27.058 --> 00:29:28.678
Your partner's your family.

630
00:29:28.679 --> 00:29:30.402
So how'd it feel
when Ethan told you

631
00:29:30.403 --> 00:29:32.195
Benny had killed your family?

632
00:29:32.196 --> 00:29:34.644
It was 15 years ago.

633
00:29:34.645 --> 00:29:36.230
Wounds heal.

634
00:29:36.231 --> 00:29:38.368
Uh. if you guys
are done trying to.

635
00:29:38.369 --> 00:29:40.161
trying to shake me down
for Benny Cohen's murder.

636
00:29:40.162 --> 00:29:41.954
I'm just gonna
get back to my game.

637
00:29:41.955 --> 00:29:43.644
Wounds heal.

638
00:29:43.645 --> 00:29:46.886
Well. why-why would
you say that wounds heal?

639
00:29:48.127 --> 00:29:51.299
This wasn't...
about revenge. Bateman.

640
00:29:51.300 --> 00:29:55.057
No. we were wrong.
This is about betrayal.

641
00:29:55.058 --> 00:29:57.816
You knew Benny
was the first suspect.

642
00:29:57.817 --> 00:30:00.437
And you also knew your partner
was on the tape. didn't you?

643
00:30:00.438 --> 00:30:02.920
Question is. when did you
find out he was dirty?

644
00:30:02.921 --> 00:30:04.161
Before or after?

645
00:30:04.162 --> 00:30:06.402
- Look. detectives--
- If somebody murdered

646
00:30:06.403 --> 00:30:08.506
my partner.
it would take 500 years

647
00:30:08.507 --> 00:30:10.678
for my wounds to heal.

648
00:30:10.679 --> 00:30:12.954
But you seem awfully copacetic.

649
00:30:12.955 --> 00:30:15.954
Copacetic with maybe
a little tinge of... guilt?

650
00:30:15.955 --> 00:30:17.609
What-what
are you suggesting?

651
00:30:17.610 --> 00:30:20.506
Officially. Vincent
was on sick leave. yeah?

652
00:30:20.507 --> 00:30:22.540
But he was actually in hiding.
wasn't he?

653
00:30:22.541 --> 00:30:25.609
The fishing cabin where
he was killed. Lake Simcoe.

654
00:30:25.610 --> 00:30:28.023
That cabin was owned
by your old captain.

655
00:30:28.024 --> 00:30:29.540
You all had access to it.

656
00:30:29.541 --> 00:30:31.954
Vincent's murder was
attributed to a string of B&Es.

657
00:30:31.955 --> 00:30:34.402
so we stopped looking at the mob

658
00:30:34.403 --> 00:30:37.506
because you made sure that
that happened. Right. Novak?

659
00:30:37.507 --> 00:30:39.057
'Cause you couldn't
have anyone asking

660
00:30:39.058 --> 00:30:41.161
how Benny knew
where Vincent was

661
00:30:41.162 --> 00:30:44.506
because Vincent didn't tell
anybody. not even his wife.

662
00:30:44.507 --> 00:30:46.851
No. But partners?

663
00:30:46.852 --> 00:30:48.989
Partners always know
more than the wives.

664
00:30:48.990 --> 00:30:51.092
Okay. look.
this-this is insane.

665
00:30:51.093 --> 00:30:54.713
Benny Cohen knew
your deepest darkest secret

666
00:30:54.714 --> 00:30:57.368
and we believe you killed him
so he wouldn't share it.

667
00:30:57.369 --> 00:30:59.368
No. No.

668
00:30:59.369 --> 00:31:02.782
For 15 years. For 15 years.
I never touched that guy.

669
00:31:04.679 --> 00:31:06.747
I didn't have to.
- What do you mean?

670
00:31:06.748 --> 00:31:08.161
Look. just to be clear.

671
00:31:08.162 --> 00:31:10.747
I'm not saying that I gave up
my partner that night.

672
00:31:10.748 --> 00:31:11.852
Th-This is...

673
00:31:13.334 --> 00:31:15.782
This is all hypothetical. right?
- Sure.

674
00:31:15.783 --> 00:31:17.057
Okay.

675
00:31:17.058 --> 00:31:19.437
Hypothetically.

676
00:31:19.438 --> 00:31:21.264
let's say...

677
00:31:21.265 --> 00:31:24.644
someone very frightening
does threaten your wife

678
00:31:24.645 --> 00:31:27.852
and your children.
and all you need to do is...

679
00:31:29.403 --> 00:31:31.851
give an address.

680
00:31:31.852 --> 00:31:34.057
A dirty cop goes down.

681
00:31:34.058 --> 00:31:36.402
And your family stays safe.

682
00:31:36.403 --> 00:31:38.195
Right?

683
00:31:38.196 --> 00:31:40.782
Let's say you are terrified.

684
00:31:40.783 --> 00:31:43.471
And let's say that you do it.

685
00:31:43.472 --> 00:31:45.264
It all goes down.
you wake up the next morning

686
00:31:45.265 --> 00:31:47.264
and your wife
brings you pancakes.

687
00:31:47.265 --> 00:31:48.747
And then she tells you
a funny story

688
00:31:48.748 --> 00:31:53.506
about leaving the key
in the lock overnight again.

689
00:31:53.507 --> 00:31:57.127
And then you realize
you are never gonna be safe.

690
00:31:58.507 --> 00:32:00.645
Not without insurance.

691
00:32:02.990 --> 00:32:04.851
So you got insurance.

692
00:32:04.852 --> 00:32:07.368
You tracked Benny.
you followed him.

693
00:32:07.369 --> 00:32:09.057
and you got a secret on him.

694
00:32:09.058 --> 00:32:12.989
What. Novak?
It's over. Benny's dead.

695
00:32:12.990 --> 00:32:14.748
You wanna tell us the secret?

696
00:32:15.369 --> 00:32:17.541
I guess it
doesn't matter anymore.

697
00:32:20.196 --> 00:32:22.920
Benny Cohen was
having an affair.

698
00:32:22.921 --> 00:32:26.954
With Rose Galatti.
Dario Galatti's wife.

699
00:32:26.955 --> 00:32:28.990
And I got pictures to prove it.

700
00:32:36.955 --> 00:32:39.471
Rose Galatti and Benny Cohen.

701
00:32:39.472 --> 00:32:41.230
These were Novak's
insurance policy.

702
00:32:41.231 --> 00:32:43.575
- Yes. they were.
- Lemme get this straight.

703
00:32:43.576 --> 00:32:46.920
Uh. Vincent O'Hagen
robs a mob stash house.

704
00:32:46.921 --> 00:32:48.885
kills five people.

705
00:32:48.886 --> 00:32:51.713
The mob hires Benny Cohen
to retaliate.

706
00:32:51.714 --> 00:32:53.816
Benny threatens
Vincent's partner

707
00:32:53.817 --> 00:32:56.023
to find out Vincent's location

708
00:32:56.024 --> 00:32:58.024
and Novak gives it up.

709
00:32:59.058 --> 00:33:01.679
A cop served up to the mob
by his partner?

710
00:33:03.990 --> 00:33:05.816
This is gonna be a garbage fire.

711
00:33:05.817 --> 00:33:07.644
Ah. it's a dirty cop
who killed a kid

712
00:33:07.645 --> 00:33:10.023
at a stash house robbery.
- I can't hear the difference.

713
00:33:10.024 --> 00:33:13.023
I'm just saying. look.
I kinda feel for Novak.

714
00:33:13.024 --> 00:33:15.576
I mean. look. if somebody
threatened my kid...

715
00:33:16.990 --> 00:33:18.644
I don't know what I would do.

716
00:33:18.645 --> 00:33:21.161
Uh. but Novak is not admitting
to anything just yet.

717
00:33:21.162 --> 00:33:23.644
But it won't take much
to prove now that we know.

718
00:33:23.645 --> 00:33:25.333
Okay. Leave it with me.

719
00:33:25.334 --> 00:33:27.402
I need to start
making some calls.

720
00:33:27.403 --> 00:33:29.333
God. is it gonna be
a long night.

721
00:33:29.334 --> 00:33:33.092
Theo. please. if you can stay
and talk this through with me.

722
00:33:33.093 --> 00:33:34.816
Mm-hmm. Of course.

723
00:33:34.817 --> 00:33:36.713
I was thrilled to get out
of that dinner.

724
00:33:36.714 --> 00:33:38.644
We need to find
Benny's killer.

725
00:33:38.645 --> 00:33:41.506
Now. I need to be able
to assure my bosses

726
00:33:41.507 --> 00:33:43.540
that no more
police were corrupted

727
00:33:43.541 --> 00:33:46.264
in the making of this movie.
- Well. Dario Galatti.

728
00:33:46.265 --> 00:33:47.954
our suspect number one.

729
00:33:47.955 --> 00:33:49.609
Mafia have a code.

730
00:33:49.610 --> 00:33:52.402
You fool around
with the boss' wife. you die.

731
00:33:52.403 --> 00:33:54.368
And more than that.
Dario trusted Benny

732
00:33:54.369 --> 00:33:56.851
as if he was his own blood.
Gave him a ring

733
00:33:56.852 --> 00:33:59.575
that normally would only go
to a made man.

734
00:33:59.576 --> 00:34:01.437
It wasn't just a gift. it was...

735
00:34:01.438 --> 00:34:03.195
It was a show of loyalty.

736
00:34:03.196 --> 00:34:04.299
an act of love.

737
00:34:04.300 --> 00:34:06.368
Now. imagine that outsider.

738
00:34:06.369 --> 00:34:08.609
the one that you've treated
like a brother.

739
00:34:08.610 --> 00:34:11.092
has been sleeping with your wife
for your entire marriage.

740
00:34:11.093 --> 00:34:12.368
Bye-bye Benny.

741
00:34:12.369 --> 00:34:14.195
Do we know where Dario
was that night?

742
00:34:14.196 --> 00:34:16.609
Alibi's rock solid.
but he's the boss.

743
00:34:16.610 --> 00:34:19.264
They seldom have blood
on their hands.

744
00:34:19.265 --> 00:34:20.954
Great we're back
to a button man.

745
00:34:20.955 --> 00:34:23.575
Who is the new Benny
in the Calabrian mob?

746
00:34:23.576 --> 00:34:25.609
Yeah. no worry.
We're on it.

747
00:34:25.610 --> 00:34:28.093
Good. I want this over.

748
00:34:35.679 --> 00:34:37.437
Thank you for the ride.
my love.

749
00:34:37.438 --> 00:34:39.437
It's fine.
I know you don't like driving.

750
00:34:39.438 --> 00:34:42.402
Hey. Matteo.
before Benny died.

751
00:34:42.403 --> 00:34:43.885
did you talk at all?

752
00:34:43.886 --> 00:34:48.368
Did he say anything strange
or out of the ordinary?

753
00:34:48.369 --> 00:34:50.506
- What do you mean?
- I don't know.

754
00:34:50.507 --> 00:34:53.644
I'm just wondering
what he was thinking.

755
00:34:53.645 --> 00:34:56.748
The day before. he asked me
to come visit him. but I...

756
00:34:57.541 --> 00:34:59.127
I didn't have time.

757
00:35:02.127 --> 00:35:04.610
I feel bad now.
- Don't feel bad.

758
00:35:05.541 --> 00:35:07.023
Benny wouldn't want that.

759
00:35:09.576 --> 00:35:11.126
<i>Grazia. amore.</i>

760
00:35:11.127 --> 00:35:13.471
Marco. the Ghost. Moretti.

761
00:35:13.472 --> 00:35:15.092
Luka. Lucky. Ferraro.

762
00:35:15.093 --> 00:35:16.678
Why does these sound
so improbable?

763
00:35:16.679 --> 00:35:18.195
Hmm. because it
doesn't line up.

764
00:35:18.196 --> 00:35:19.989
Well.

765
00:35:19.990 --> 00:35:22.989
I meant their names. but. uh.
what're you talking about?

766
00:35:22.990 --> 00:35:24.885
Benny's death.

767
00:35:24.886 --> 00:35:27.333
You know. if we're right
about the motives.

768
00:35:27.334 --> 00:35:30.195
then this was personal.

769
00:35:30.196 --> 00:35:34.816
This wasn't about business
or. uh. rivalry. or greed.

770
00:35:34.817 --> 00:35:39.264
This was betrayal
of a Shakespearean proportion.

771
00:35:39.265 --> 00:35:40.816
You think Dario
did it himself?

772
00:35:40.817 --> 00:35:42.402
It was too personal not to.

773
00:35:42.403 --> 00:35:44.644
Maybe. except.
uh. Il macellaio.

774
00:35:44.645 --> 00:35:48.506
I mean. pushing an old man out
in the cold to freeze to death?

775
00:35:48.507 --> 00:35:50.506
No. it's a little tame
for a man

776
00:35:50.507 --> 00:35:52.644
who was known
for flaying people.

777
00:35:55.024 --> 00:35:57.748
You know. it almost looks like
the work of a civilian.

778
00:35:59.921 --> 00:36:01.851
- Like his son. maybe?
- Yeah. but I thought Matteo

779
00:36:01.852 --> 00:36:03.989
wasn't following
in his father's footsteps.

780
00:36:03.990 --> 00:36:06.437
Yeah. except Benny
was sleeping with his mother.

781
00:36:06.438 --> 00:36:09.402
humiliating his father.
and maybe that was enough to...

782
00:36:09.403 --> 00:36:12.230
Bring him back home.

783
00:36:12.231 --> 00:36:13.885
Pull him back in?

784
00:36:13.886 --> 00:36:18.023
As you can see. the old owners
didn't like cheap things.

785
00:36:18.024 --> 00:36:20.333
And there's nothing cheap
about this view.

786
00:36:20.334 --> 00:36:21.989
Or these floors.

787
00:36:21.990 --> 00:36:24.402
These babies.
- Blonde maple?

788
00:36:24.403 --> 00:36:25.540
Hand-milled?

789
00:36:25.541 --> 00:36:27.092
That's very good.

790
00:36:27.093 --> 00:36:29.195
- He likes to show off.
- I do.

791
00:36:29.196 --> 00:36:30.955
Especially this little guy.

792
00:36:31.921 --> 00:36:33.161
Do you mind?

793
00:36:33.162 --> 00:36:34.816
Why don't you go check out
the wine cellar?

794
00:36:34.817 --> 00:36:36.576
I'll be down in a second.

795
00:36:38.472 --> 00:36:39.885
Detective.

796
00:36:39.886 --> 00:36:41.540
I'm not sure
if you've heard.

797
00:36:41.541 --> 00:36:43.230
but I don't bake.

798
00:36:43.231 --> 00:36:45.471
Maybe not. but.
well. you did assault a man

799
00:36:45.472 --> 00:36:48.299
when you were 15 for
insulting your father. was it?

800
00:36:48.300 --> 00:36:50.678
And on the night
that Benny Cohen died.

801
00:36:50.679 --> 00:36:54.748
your car was a block away
from Gracewood Manor.

802
00:36:58.024 --> 00:37:00.230
Seems Orwell was right.

803
00:37:00.231 --> 00:37:01.713
Big Brother is watching.

804
00:37:01.714 --> 00:37:03.437
Well. he can watch
what he likes.

805
00:37:03.438 --> 00:37:05.126
because I was home
asleep that night.

806
00:37:05.127 --> 00:37:08.092
So. your car
just wandered off?

807
00:37:08.093 --> 00:37:11.126
Benny saved my life.
He was like an uncle to me.

808
00:37:11.127 --> 00:37:12.816
And I've seen that trick before.
you've been playing it

809
00:37:12.817 --> 00:37:14.644
on my family for years.
Get a new one.

810
00:37:14.645 --> 00:37:16.161
That photo is real.

811
00:37:16.162 --> 00:37:19.092
so we could get a warrant
for the GPS to corroborate it.

812
00:37:19.093 --> 00:37:20.678
or you could just
tell us the truth.

813
00:37:20.679 --> 00:37:22.333
Save everyone a lot of trouble.

814
00:37:22.334 --> 00:37:24.713
I was home. I swear to you.

815
00:37:24.714 --> 00:37:25.989
Matteo. wait.

816
00:37:25.990 --> 00:37:28.333
Did Benny tell you something
before he died?

817
00:37:28.334 --> 00:37:30.471
Did he try to...
pull you aside. maybe?

818
00:37:30.472 --> 00:37:32.920
No? No. why does everyone
keep asking me that?

819
00:37:32.921 --> 00:37:34.161
Who's everyone?

820
00:37:37.127 --> 00:37:40.092
You know what?
You wanna keep chatting?

821
00:37:40.093 --> 00:37:42.541
Talk to my lawyer.
We're done.

822
00:37:44.541 --> 00:37:46.437
Okay. Graff. what's going on?

823
00:37:46.438 --> 00:37:48.541
Well.
kid just showed his hand.

824
00:37:51.265 --> 00:37:52.437
We're closed!

825
00:37:52.438 --> 00:37:54.023
Well. we're not here
for the crostini.

826
00:37:54.024 --> 00:37:55.540
as delicious as they are.

827
00:37:55.541 --> 00:37:57.954
Ma. you're
almost ready to head home?

828
00:37:57.955 --> 00:37:59.851
If you're looking for Dario.
he's not--

829
00:37:59.852 --> 00:38:01.437
We're not here
for Dario either.

830
00:38:01.438 --> 00:38:02.954
We'd like to talk
to you and your son.

831
00:38:02.955 --> 00:38:04.506
And let's hope
for all our sakes

832
00:38:04.507 --> 00:38:08.402
that this conversation ends
before your husband arrives.

833
00:38:10.783 --> 00:38:12.299
Ah. there he is.

834
00:38:12.300 --> 00:38:14.162
Prodigal son.

835
00:38:15.231 --> 00:38:18.195
I told you this afternoon.
talk to my lawyer.

836
00:38:18.196 --> 00:38:21.230
We will. We just wanted
to clear a few things up first.

837
00:38:21.231 --> 00:38:24.609
Yeah. I find baking
an interesting choice of front

838
00:38:24.610 --> 00:38:27.816
for organized crime. hmm?

839
00:38:27.817 --> 00:38:30.230
Bread.

840
00:38:30.231 --> 00:38:31.921
Mana.

841
00:38:32.714 --> 00:38:33.989
Food from the gods.

842
00:38:33.990 --> 00:38:38.023
All made possible
by a reaction of yeast

843
00:38:38.024 --> 00:38:40.471
feeding on sugar. a fungus

844
00:38:40.472 --> 00:38:44.023
getting rich off the sweet
of the innocent.

845
00:38:44.024 --> 00:38:47.506
Carnage in history
created by something as simple

846
00:38:47.507 --> 00:38:50.402
as mixing
flour with water.

847
00:38:53.438 --> 00:38:56.575
You see. baking has a recipe.

848
00:38:56.576 --> 00:38:58.161
and the mafia has a code.

849
00:38:58.162 --> 00:39:01.437
Strict rules of loyalty
and retribution.

850
00:39:01.438 --> 00:39:03.023
And if those rules
aren't followed

851
00:39:03.024 --> 00:39:05.230
as closely
as the recipe. well...

852
00:39:05.231 --> 00:39:07.782
it's mayhem.
- But I can't hope but notice

853
00:39:07.783 --> 00:39:09.885
that brown mark
on your hand. Matteo.

854
00:39:09.886 --> 00:39:11.747
- My hand?
- Yeah. you have another one

855
00:39:11.748 --> 00:39:13.885
on your neck. probably have
a few more on your chest.

856
00:39:13.886 --> 00:39:15.713
might wanna see a doctor.
- I did.

857
00:39:15.714 --> 00:39:17.264
They said they're just
birthmarks.

858
00:39:17.265 --> 00:39:18.816
Well. that's because
you didn't know

859
00:39:18.817 --> 00:39:22.092
that one of your parents
had neurofibromatosis.

860
00:39:22.093 --> 00:39:24.816
It's passed down from
a parent to a child.

861
00:39:24.817 --> 00:39:27.713
- Detectives... please.
- My parents don't have that.

862
00:39:27.714 --> 00:39:28.610
Ma?

863
00:39:30.369 --> 00:39:31.920
Is that what Benny had?

864
00:39:31.921 --> 00:39:33.299
That's why
he had trouble walking.

865
00:39:33.300 --> 00:39:34.954
He had a tumour in his spine.

866
00:39:34.955 --> 00:39:37.989
Ma. What are you saying?

867
00:39:37.990 --> 00:39:41.644
I think you know
what she's saying. Matteo.

868
00:39:41.645 --> 00:39:44.989
Maybe you've always known it.
deep down. that Benny

869
00:39:44.990 --> 00:39:47.886
is your biological father.

870
00:39:49.196 --> 00:39:51.575
And you. Prim.

871
00:39:51.576 --> 00:39:52.885
Primrose.

872
00:39:52.886 --> 00:39:54.264
the girl that Benny

873
00:39:54.265 --> 00:39:56.230
could never stop pining for.

874
00:39:56.231 --> 00:39:58.782
You know. when I found out
that Benny had been drugged.

875
00:39:58.783 --> 00:40:02.402
I assumed the killer was just
wanting to keep him quiet.

876
00:40:02.403 --> 00:40:04.885
but it was really an act
of kindness. wasn't it. Matteo?

877
00:40:04.886 --> 00:40:07.575
You knew Benny had to go.

878
00:40:07.576 --> 00:40:09.747
Before Dario found out
the truth.

879
00:40:09.748 --> 00:40:12.092
Because loose lips.
they sink ships.

880
00:40:12.093 --> 00:40:14.402
But even so. you didn't
want Benny to suffer.

881
00:40:14.403 --> 00:40:16.368
'Cause you loved him.
didn't you?

882
00:40:16.369 --> 00:40:19.920
Like only a son can.
- What? No!

883
00:40:19.921 --> 00:40:22.126
Your car was a block
away from Gracewood

884
00:40:22.127 --> 00:40:23.575
the night that Benny
was killed.

885
00:40:23.576 --> 00:40:25.609
You can't account for your
whereabouts on that night

886
00:40:25.610 --> 00:40:27.299
and now. look at that.
we have a motive.

887
00:40:27.300 --> 00:40:28.989
- No. please--
- I think it's about time

888
00:40:28.990 --> 00:40:31.471
we call your lawyer.
- No! Ma-Matteo wasn't driving

889
00:40:31.472 --> 00:40:33.576
his car that night. I was.

890
00:40:38.817 --> 00:40:41.747
I took it out of the driveway.
he has nothing to do with this.

891
00:40:41.748 --> 00:40:43.747
Matteo. please. go wait
in the front. alright--

892
00:40:43.748 --> 00:40:45.609
No. I'm not going anywhere.
Please. someone explain

893
00:40:45.610 --> 00:40:48.886
to me what is going on?!
- Benny was saying things.

894
00:40:49.645 --> 00:40:51.816
Secret things.

895
00:40:51.817 --> 00:40:54.126
Things that...
if Dario found out--

896
00:40:54.127 --> 00:40:56.782
Dario would have
to honour the code

897
00:40:56.783 --> 00:40:58.333
and kill his beloved friend

898
00:40:58.334 --> 00:41:00.230
in the most gruesome
way possible.

899
00:41:00.231 --> 00:41:01.782
If Benny knew
what he was doing.

900
00:41:01.783 --> 00:41:03.713
betraying the promises
we made to each other.

901
00:41:03.714 --> 00:41:05.540
he would have done it himself.

902
00:41:05.541 --> 00:41:06.817
You don't know that.

903
00:41:09.058 --> 00:41:12.092
You can't know what
was in his mind. No one can.

904
00:41:12.093 --> 00:41:15.437
And dementia or not.
these people are still in there.

905
00:41:15.438 --> 00:41:17.333
They still appreciate kindness.

906
00:41:17.334 --> 00:41:19.333
They still feel love--

907
00:41:19.334 --> 00:41:22.471
So what?
Let him be butchered?

908
00:41:22.472 --> 00:41:24.195
When you work for my husband.

909
00:41:24.196 --> 00:41:27.954
he puts a card in your hand
and lights it on fire.

910
00:41:27.955 --> 00:41:31.126
And says. as this card burns.

911
00:41:31.127 --> 00:41:33.816
so will you burn alive
if you betray me.

912
00:41:33.817 --> 00:41:35.471
And he means it.

913
00:41:35.472 --> 00:41:38.092
So you tell me.
what was I supposed to do?

914
00:41:38.093 --> 00:41:40.023
Let my son be burned alive?

915
00:41:40.024 --> 00:41:42.092
Let him see his mother die?

916
00:41:42.093 --> 00:41:44.678
Let my husband torture
Benny to death?

917
00:41:44.679 --> 00:41:47.748
Oh. so you just left him out
in the cold instead?

918
00:41:48.783 --> 00:41:51.231
- It wasn't like that.
- No?

919
00:41:52.507 --> 00:41:54.162
I went by his side.

920
00:41:55.852 --> 00:41:58.195
I played our favourite song.

921
00:41:58.196 --> 00:42:00.713
Poured him his
favourite scotch and.

922
00:42:00.714 --> 00:42:03.748
and made it so that
he wouldn't feel pain.

923
00:42:06.472 --> 00:42:08.644
And I held his hand

924
00:42:08.645 --> 00:42:10.644
as long as I could

925
00:42:10.645 --> 00:42:12.127
before...

926
00:42:16.334 --> 00:42:19.024
What I did was a mercy.

927
00:42:19.921 --> 00:42:23.402
And maybe so.
But it was also murder.

928
00:42:24.748 --> 00:42:27.023
Please. Detective.
let my mother go.

929
00:42:27.024 --> 00:42:29.437
Okay. Take me. We'll say
that it was an argument.

930
00:42:29.438 --> 00:42:31.437
A debt that
Benny couldn't pay.

931
00:42:31.438 --> 00:42:33.402
We'll say that I did it!
If my father finds out

932
00:42:33.403 --> 00:42:35.851
about this...
- If Father finds out what?

933
00:42:35.852 --> 00:42:37.506
What's going on here?

934
00:42:37.507 --> 00:42:38.920
Dad.

935
00:42:38.921 --> 00:42:40.747
Let's... let's go outside.

936
00:42:40.748 --> 00:42:43.747
let them finish up. yeah?
- What's going on here. Rose?

937
00:42:58.403 --> 00:43:00.092
What do you think
Dario's gonna do

938
00:43:00.093 --> 00:43:02.471
now that he knows
who Matteo really is?

939
00:43:02.472 --> 00:43:05.264
Gonna stick with the code?
Destroy his own son?

940
00:43:05.265 --> 00:43:08.471
Ah. I hope not.
Codes. vows. words.

941
00:43:08.472 --> 00:43:10.782
There's one thing you learn

942
00:43:10.783 --> 00:43:12.576
on the job. it's that...

943
00:43:13.783 --> 00:43:15.575
Everything can be broken.

944
00:43:29.645 --> 00:43:33.403
difuze

945
00:43:34.305 --> 00:44:34.917
